P5W PATCH 01 (Desktop only) - I "Revenue by tenor": average tenor inside each bar in the tooltip      BUILD 2026-11-11a
=====================================================================================================================
2 NEW measures in table _Measures + 1 visual step. No table or column. Reads the existing [P5 Tenor Text]
(nominal-weighted average of DealLifeDays, rows with nominal <= the EUR 50bn cap - same rule as the scorecard
"avg tenor" column), so the tooltip and Z1 always agree.
 
NEW measure : select table _Measures > Table tools > New measure > Ctrl+A > paste the block > Enter.
              Then (Measure tools ribbon) Display folder P5\2 Product, format Text.
UNDO: delete the two measures.
 
==== 1/2  NEW
P5 I Tenor Bar =
-- Average tenor of the WHOLE bar under the cursor (all product line groups in that tenor bucket), whatever segment
-- is hovered. ALLSELECTED keeps the page / slicer / cross-filter selection and only drops the segment's own
-- line-group filter. Example on 5Y: "3.2y" tells you whether the bucket is mostly 2y or mostly 4y deals.
CALCULATE ( [P5 Tenor Text], ALLSELECTED ( DIM_PRODUCTLINE ) )
 
==== 2/2  NEW
P5 I Tenor Product =
-- Average tenor of the hovered segment only (that product line group, in that tenor bucket).
[P5 Tenor Text]
 
==== VISUAL STEP - I Tenor tooltip
1. Select I (Revenue by tenor) > Build pane > Tooltips well: drag in P5 I Tenor Bar, then P5 I Tenor Product.
2. Rename them in the well (double-click): "Avg tenor · whole bar" and "Avg tenor · this product".
3. Hover the 5Y bar on any segment -> tooltip reads, for example:
     Tenor Bucket          5Y
     ProductLineGroupName  EUR RATES
     P5 Revenue            €98.4m
     Avg tenor · whole bar     3.1y
     Avg tenor · this product  4.2y
   (Figures are an illustration, not reference values.)
 
==== CHECKS (P5W_PATCH_01_CHECK.dax, part T1)
T1 Per bucket, 2026 YTD, Exclude: average tenor sits inside the bucket's range (5Y between 1.0y and 5.0y, 30Y between
   10y and 50y). A figure outside its range = rows with no nominal or above the cap dominate that bucket - flag it.



// =====================================================================================
// P5W_PATCH_01_CHECK.dax  -  BUILD 2026-11-11a  -  read-only
// T1  tenor tooltip: average tenor per bucket (whole book) and per bucket x line group.
// T2  scorecard (Z1) vs mix-by-year (F) per year: where the gap comes from.
// RUN: DAX query view > paste > Run. 3 result tabs. Intra-group = Exclude (the page default).
// =====================================================================================
DEFINE
    VAR _ytd = DATESBETWEEN ( DIM_DATE[Date], DATE ( 2026, 1, 1 ), DATE ( 2026, 12, 31 ) )
    VAR _excl = TREATAS ( { "Exclude" }, 'P5W IntraGroup'[Option] )

// ---- T1a  per tenor bucket, whole book, 2026 YTD ------------------------------------------------------
EVALUATE
    SUMMARIZECOLUMNS (
        FACT_SALES[Tenor Bucket Sort], FACT_SALES[Tenor Bucket],
        _ytd, _excl,
        "Revenue", [P5 Revenue],
        "TenorDays", [P5 Tenor Days],
        "Tenor", [P5 Tenor Text]
    )
    ORDER BY FACT_SALES[Tenor Bucket Sort]

// ---- T1b  5Y bucket by line group (what the tooltip shows segment by segment) -------------------------
EVALUATE
    SUMMARIZECOLUMNS (
        DIM_PRODUCTLINE[ProductLineGroupName],
        TREATAS ( { "5Y" }, FACT_SALES[Tenor Bucket] ),
        _ytd, _excl,
        "Revenue", [P5 Revenue],
        "TenorThisProduct", [P5 Tenor Text],
        "TenorWholeBar", CALCULATE ( [P5 Tenor Text], ALLSELECTED ( DIM_PRODUCTLINE ) )
    )
    ORDER BY [Revenue] DESC

// ---- T2  Z1 vs F per year ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FullYear  = what Z1 shows with the period slicer on that whole calendar year.
// F_SP      = what F shows for that year (1 Jan -> same day/month as the last sales date).
// Gap       = FullYear - F_SP = revenue booked after that day/month (expected > 0 for every past year, 0 for 2026).
// NoFamily  = revenue whose line group has no Family (would sit in a (Blank) segment of F).
EVALUATE
    ADDCOLUMNS (
        SELECTCOLUMNS ( GENERATESERIES ( 2023, 2026, 1 ), "Year", [Value] ),
        "FullYear", VAR y = [Year] RETURN CALCULATE ( [P5 Revenue], _excl, REMOVEFILTERS ( DIM_DATE ), DIM_DATE[Year] = y ),
        "F_SP", VAR y = [Year] RETURN CALCULATE ( [P5 F Revenue SP], _excl, REMOVEFILTERS ( DIM_DATE ), DIM_DATE[Year] = y ),
        "Gap", VAR y = [Year] RETURN
            CALCULATE ( [P5 Revenue], _excl, REMOVEFILTERS ( DIM_DATE ), DIM_DATE[Year] = y )
                - CALCULATE ( [P5 F Revenue SP], _excl, REMOVEFILTERS ( DIM_DATE ), DIM_DATE[Year] = y ),
        "NoFamily", VAR y = [Year] RETURN
            CALCULATE ( [P5 Revenue], _excl, REMOVEFILTERS ( DIM_DATE ), DIM_DATE[Year] = y,
                FILTER ( ALL ( DIM_PRODUCTLINE[Family] ), ISBLANK ( DIM_PRODUCTLINE[Family] ) || DIM_PRODUCTLINE[Family] = "" ) ),
        "CutDate", FORMAT ( [Asof Sales Date], "d mmm" )
    )
